WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.080
This is part two of the practice set,

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.400
with questions three and four.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.720
The method is the same as part one:

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:09.200
divide by the volume first, then the I

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.920
C E table, I for initial, C for

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.480
change, E for equilibrium.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.440
Question three gives K for the other equation,

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.200
so you will have to flip it, and

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.600
its K is tiny, so the 5 per

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.840
cent check goes on the amount actually taken

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.280
off, which here is two x.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.720
Question four has two parts: part a finds

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.120
K, and part b hides a perfect square.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:35.440
Pause and try each one, then we'll work

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.040
it through one step at a time.

00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:39.426
Question three.

00:00:39.707 --> 00:00:42.426
For two N O plus chlorine making two

00:00:42.587 --> 00:00:46.186
N O C L, nitrosyl chloride, K is

00:00:46.307 --> 00:00:48.946
6.25 times ten to the four at a

00:00:48.987 --> 00:00:50.306
certain temperature.

00:00:50.747 --> 00:00:53.786
2.00 moles of N O C L is

00:00:53.947 --> 00:00:57.226
placed in an empty 4.00 litre vessel at

00:00:57.347 --> 00:00:59.946
that temperature, and some of it splits.

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:02.426
How many moles of chlorine are present at

00:01:02.507 --> 00:01:03.226
equilibrium?

00:01:03.787 --> 00:01:05.146
Pause here to answer.

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:17.886
Look at which way the equation runs.

00:01:18.127 --> 00:01:20.206
K was given for the equation that makes

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:23.246
N O C L, but this vessel starts

00:01:23.327 --> 00:01:25.566
with N O C L, which splits.

00:01:25.887 --> 00:01:27.806
K belongs to the equation as it is

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.366
written, so write the equation the way this

00:01:30.447 --> 00:01:33.326
vessel runs, and flip K with it: one

00:01:33.487 --> 00:01:36.446
over 6.25 times ten to the four is

00:01:36.527 --> 00:01:39.566
1.6 times ten to the minus five, which

00:01:39.647 --> 00:01:40.726
is tiny.

00:01:41.087 --> 00:01:43.726
Question two ran backwards too, but we kept

00:01:43.807 --> 00:01:46.206
its equation as given, so its K stayed

00:01:46.287 --> 00:01:47.406
the same.

00:01:47.527 --> 00:01:48.686
Now the table.

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:53.886
The start is 2.00 over 4.00, 0.500

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:56.526
moles per litre.

00:01:56.647 --> 00:01:59.326
If x of chlorine forms, then two x

00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:01.406
of N O C L splits and two

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:04.206
x of N O forms, so the equilibrium

00:02:04.287 --> 00:02:09.006
row is 0.500 minus two x, two x,

00:02:09.087 --> 00:02:09.806
and x.

00:02:11.034 --> 00:02:14.313
K is two x all squared, times x,

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:19.353
over 0.500 minus two x, all squared.

00:02:19.474 --> 00:02:22.793
K is tiny, so very little splits: drop

00:02:22.874 --> 00:02:24.473
the two x from the bottom, and keep

00:02:24.554 --> 00:02:26.393
the x on top, because that is the

00:02:26.474 --> 00:02:27.513
answer.

00:02:27.594 --> 00:02:33.513
The bottom becomes 0.500 squared, 0.250.

00:02:33.594 --> 00:02:36.873
On top, two x all squared, times x,

00:02:36.954 --> 00:02:38.713
is four x cubed.

00:02:38.954 --> 00:02:43.193
Multiply both sides by the bottom, 0.250: four

00:02:43.274 --> 00:02:45.993
x cubed is 4.0 times ten to the

00:02:46.074 --> 00:02:47.433
minus six.

00:02:47.554 --> 00:02:50.633
Then divide both sides by four: x cubed

00:02:50.714 --> 00:02:53.593
is 1.0 times ten to the minus six,

00:02:53.714 --> 00:02:56.953
and x is 0.0100.

00:02:58.167 --> 00:02:59.286
Check the shortcut.

00:02:59.687 --> 00:03:01.846
The amount taken off the start is two

00:03:01.927 --> 00:03:06.566
x, not x: 0.0200 out of

00:03:06.647 --> 00:03:10.086
0.500 is 4 per cent.

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:13.126
That is under about 5, so it passes,

00:03:13.207 --> 00:03:14.486
but only just.

00:03:15.047 --> 00:03:19.686
Chlorine is 0.0100 moles per litre, times 4.00

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:24.886
litres, which is 0.0400 moles.

00:03:24.967 --> 00:03:28.086
The classic mistake is putting 6.25 times ten

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:30.726
to the four into the splitting expression without

00:03:30.807 --> 00:03:31.846
flipping it.

00:03:31.927 --> 00:03:34.086
That gives x of about 16 moles per

00:03:34.207 --> 00:03:37.926
litre, far more than the 0.500 you started

00:03:38.007 --> 00:03:39.606
with, which is impossible.

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:42.833
Question four has two parts.

00:03:43.474 --> 00:03:46.993
Nitrogen dioxide and sulfur dioxide react to make

00:03:47.074 --> 00:03:51.393
nitrogen monoxide and sulfur trioxide, all gases.

00:03:51.714 --> 00:03:56.193
At 460 degrees, a 5.00 litre vessel at

00:03:56.274 --> 00:04:01.233
equilibrium holds 0.100 moles of N O two,

00:04:01.354 --> 00:04:06.273
0.200 of S O two, 0.900 of

00:04:06.354 --> 00:04:10.073
N O and 1.80 of S O three.

00:04:10.434 --> 00:04:12.793
Part a: calculate K.

00:04:13.074 --> 00:04:14.353
Pause here to answer.

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:31.006
Divide each amount by 5.00: 0.0200,

00:04:31.127 --> 00:04:35.726
0.0400, 0.180 and

00:04:35.847 --> 00:04:38.766
0.360 moles per litre.

00:04:39.327 --> 00:04:42.686
Every coefficient is one, so K is N

00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:45.406
O times S O three, over N O

00:04:45.487 --> 00:04:47.126
two times S O two.

00:04:47.407 --> 00:04:52.206
On top, 0.180 times 0.360 is

00:04:52.327 --> 00:04:54.766
0.0648.

00:04:54.847 --> 00:05:01.006
Underneath, 0.0200 times 0.0400 is

00:05:01.127 --> 00:05:04.526
0.000800.

00:05:04.647 --> 00:05:07.246
So K is 81.0.

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:09.546
Part b.

00:05:09.827 --> 00:05:13.826
At the same temperature, 0.500 moles of N

00:05:13.907 --> 00:05:17.746
O two and 0.500 moles of S O

00:05:17.867 --> 00:05:21.266
two are placed in an empty 2.00 litre

00:05:21.347 --> 00:05:22.386
vessel.

00:05:22.507 --> 00:05:24.546
Find the concentration of N O two at

00:05:24.627 --> 00:05:25.906
equilibrium.

00:05:26.067 --> 00:05:27.266
Pause here to answer.

00:05:37.667 --> 00:05:41.746
Same temperature, so the same K: 81.0 from

00:05:41.827 --> 00:05:42.746
part a.

00:05:43.027 --> 00:05:46.706
The start is 0.250 of each reactant.

00:05:47.267 --> 00:05:49.986
Each reactant changes by minus x, and each

00:05:50.147 --> 00:05:51.586
product by plus x.

00:05:52.147 --> 00:05:55.426
So K is x times x, over 0.250

00:05:55.507 --> 00:06:00.146
minus x, times 0.250 minus x.

00:06:00.707 --> 00:06:03.026
That looks like it needs the quadratic formula.

00:06:03.427 --> 00:06:04.946
You can use it if you like, but

00:06:05.027 --> 00:06:07.506
HSC questions are written so you shouldn't need

00:06:07.587 --> 00:06:08.786
it, so look again.

00:06:09.267 --> 00:06:11.746
The top is x squared, and the bottom

00:06:11.907 --> 00:06:15.346
is 0.250 minus x, all squared.

00:06:15.907 --> 00:06:17.826
It is a perfect square, because the two

00:06:17.907 --> 00:06:19.586
reactants started equal.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:23.600
Take the square root of both sides: x

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:28.480
over 0.250 minus x is 9.00.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:33.120
Multiply both sides by the bottom, 0.250 minus

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:37.600
x: x equals 2.25 minus 9 x.

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:40.320
Add 9 x to both sides, so ten

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:44.720
x is 2.25, then divide by ten: x

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:46.920
is 0.225.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:49.600
But the question asks for N O two,

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:55.680
which is 0.250 minus x: 0.0250 moles

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:56.320
per litre.

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:02.240
Check: 0.225 squared over 0.0250 squared

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:03.680
is 81.

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:06.160
The classic mistake is stopping at x and

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:09.200
giving 0.225 as the answer.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:11.440
x is the change, not the N O

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:12.000
two.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.800
So here is what to look for.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:18.320
K for a different equation: flip it if

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:21.040
the equation is reversed, square it if it

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:22.000
is doubled.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:24.880
K and a start: look for a perfect

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:27.520
square, or a tiny K with the 5

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:29.880
per cent check on the amount taken off.

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:33.120
Asked for moles: convert back at the end,

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.520
and answer what was asked, because x is

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:36.480
the change.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:39.360
And two parts at the same temperature use

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:40.400
the same K.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.840
Next: how temperature changes K.

00:07:45.067 --> 00:07:46.506
Here are the key notes.

00:07:46.747 --> 00:07:48.666
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:48.747 --> 00:07:49.546
to copy them.
